 holds no agent text or host paths. Scanner failure streaks (#221, the early slice of the digest, #58): each scanner posts one comment on the status issue when a failure streak starts and one when it recovers. A streak starts at the first run that is a guard trip or guard error (reason: the guard rule name or `scan-error`), any other `scan_failed` run (a `timeout` counts as `scan_failed`) or a skip at `max_open`, and ends at the next `ok` run. The posted class is kept in the scanner's `meta` table (key `failure_streak`), so a restart does not repost, and it is written only after the post succeeds. Runs dropped at the global cap and `error` runs neither start nor end a streak. A comment carries the scanner name and the reason class only, never finding text, titles, fingerprints or log lines. The post goes through the effect layer, so a dry-run logs it (`scanner.streak_notice`) and stores no streak. While the status issue number is unknown nothing is posted and the streak is not recorded, so it posts once the issue exists.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a28b173e-239b-4d03-87ce-1ee0fe9c79f6","uuid":"c3f347c9-4854-4ca1-ba52-4ab12eb92a36","timestamp":"2026-11-25T15:02:00.077Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---\nrole: lead\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\nnext: [triage:engineer]\nworker: engineer\n---\nAdds a read-only terminal UI to ard serve that draws the slice 1 snapshot, sends logs to a file while it runs, and keeps today's output when there is no TTY. The engineer triage role writes the plan and the engineer worker implements it. This repository has no architect, designer or documentation triage role, so the engineer plan has to cover the new dependency, the layout and the proposal paragraph too.\n\n## Routing\n- triage:engineer: implementation steps for TTY detection, log redirection, panel rendering, key handling and sanitisation, plus the golden-frame and key-handling test plan and the dependency pins.\n- worker engineer: Go code, tests and